erid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-02-2017, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T02:46:17-07:00","id":1123809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1117619-dark-eras-early-middle-ages-resources?p=1123807#post1123807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditional Gaelic ( Scotish ) Names - <a href=\"http://www.namenerds.com/scottish/gaelicdude.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.namenerds.com/scottish/gaelicdude.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I created simple Name Generator from this nice Table - I putted in spreadsheet it's content and added rows numbers. Now I have 203 names with numbers to let me roll d203 in any diceroller to have random Gaelic name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Total Random Generator - <a href=\"https://www.random.org/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.random.org/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-02-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T05:11:34-07:00","id":1123835,"title":"","content":"Prepared some NPCs names for story on those lists. In monastery are more brothers ( probably circa 40 men ) but those are placeholders names for needed NPCs in scenes.<br /> <br /> <b>Monstery</b><br /> <b>Abbot</b> <b>Donnan</b><br /> <b>Brothers:</b> Athairne, Bearchan, Brandubh, Coireall, Drostan, Laise, Machar, Onchu, Ros, Uallas<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vampires</span></b><br /> All three are Nosferatus from Lancea Sanctum, masquareding as leper brothers in Abbey.<ul><li><b>Ambrosius</b></li> <li><b>Clement</b></li> <li><b>Mauris</b></li> </ul>Now need only name for native Uratha in nearby forest...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T11:30:37-07:00","id":1215563,"title":"","content":"Found today great site - Ancient.eu - that makes nicely readable in plain language articles on almost all historical topics. It's co-run with Oxford University. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ancient.eu/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:32:50-07:00","id":1221755,"title":"","content":"Found great page for marking of time relation to the geopolitical situation in Middle Ages - <b><a href=\"https://www.timemaps.com/history/\" target=\"_blank\">Timemaps Archive</a></b>. Just point nearest date on the list and you can see how looked whole world in that time. Great visualization of context for historical games! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}